Phase 2 Task 3: Unify GPS stationaryWeight onto motionStillness.

Red (baseline guards): two tests written and run against the OLD inline
ramp — both passed (guards, not discriminators; the plan scopes this task
as no-regression at rest-exit and cruise):
- 'should zero-blend GPS velocity at rest and restore it after rest-exit
  (unified stationaryWeight)': at rest (motionStillness = 1) a sub-floor
  spurious GPS Doppler (+0.5 m/s, below GPS_REST_NOISE = 1.0) must not be
  adopted (v < 0.5) and ms > 0.9; after green-light ramp to 5 m/s the
  velocity returns at full weight (v > 3.5). NOTE: first draft used a
  consistent +2 m/s bias which FAILED because lastGpsSpeed = 2 legitimately
  reads as motion via the hybrid-speed EMA — a real red-light residual sits
  below the rest-noise floor, so the premise was corrected to 0.5 m/s.
- 'should use GPS velocity at full weight at cruise': mounted 8 m/s cruise,
  ms < 0.1, v > 7.5.

Green: updateGps() now computes stationaryWeight = this.motionStillness
instead of the inline (threshold - smoothedSpeed)/threshold ramp, and the
updateMotionStillness() call moved BEFORE the blend (was after the block;
the metric is fed by the same smoothedSpeed EMA, so value is identical).
Removed the duplicate updateMotionStillness() call at the old site.

Behavioral change: the ramp location shifts from [0,1] m/s (inline) to
[1,2] m/s (ms = 1 - max(0, smoothedSpeed - GPS_REST_NOISE)) — at/below 1
m/s the velocity is now fully zero-blended and velR capped at 5x; the
transition happens over 1-2 m/s. Bounded impact because ZUPT (also gated
on ms) dominates <= ~1.85 m/s. Heading cross-row decoupling
S[PSI][X/Y/V] *= (1-w) now tracks ms identically.

Transient note: on the FIRST GPS fix after a gap while this.coasting is
still true, the metric takes the stale branch (filter v + forward proxy)
so sw may differ from the old smoothedSpeed value for that one fix; the
coast-recovery resetFromGps path self-corrects if the gate fails.

